1
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:40,041
[SPEAKER_00]: We were speaking about saṅkharas earlier, and how it's usually translated, well, how we were translating it in the past with determinations, but you seem to be translating it now as activities.

2
00:00:40,681 --> 00:00:41,401
[SPEAKER_01]: Activations?

3
00:00:41,501 --> 00:00:42,082
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

4
00:00:43,082 --> 00:00:49,566
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, well, see, the problem with it is just, as I said before, when you look into the suttas, there's often

5
00:00:52,988 --> 00:01:02,652
[SPEAKER_01]: There's often a very practical instructions given by the Buddha, how, you know, how to, like, how to calm the saṅkharas, how to regard them, and so on.

6
00:01:04,012 --> 00:01:10,275
[SPEAKER_01]: But, any other way, it just was not, any other translation, it just wasn't practical enough.

7
00:01:10,515 --> 00:01:11,975
[SPEAKER_01]: How to calm determinations.

8
00:01:12,216 --> 00:01:14,416
[SPEAKER_00]: But, I'll just refrain from determining.

9
00:01:14,476 --> 00:01:15,477
[SPEAKER_00]: But, what is it?

10
00:01:15,917 --> 00:01:17,158
[SPEAKER_01]: How am I determining things?

11
00:01:17,178 --> 00:01:18,218
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not determining anything.

12
00:01:19,390 --> 00:01:22,894
[SPEAKER_01]: Or even more ambiguous formations, mental formations.

13
00:01:23,054 --> 00:01:24,876
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, everything is a mental formation.

14
00:01:24,936 --> 00:01:26,197
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything is a saṅkhara.

15
00:01:27,939 --> 00:01:32,323
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, but so what... how do I... so under that same mental level, what do I do?

16
00:01:33,004 --> 00:01:34,305
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the suttas talk about it.

17
00:01:34,325 --> 00:01:38,249
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha gives examples of calming saṅkharas.

18
00:01:38,269 --> 00:01:40,632
[SPEAKER_01]: And calming saṅkhara basically equates with samādhi.

19
00:01:43,548 --> 00:01:49,712
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, just practically, I was looking practically into it, how would you convey that, which saṅkharas are?

20
00:01:49,732 --> 00:02:03,320
[SPEAKER_01]: You could just say saṅkharas, you know, if a person knows what saṅkharas are, that's fine, but if somebody is still not familiar, yeah, it is obviously, you know, sabhe-saṅkhara, anicca, sabhe-saṅkhara, dukkha, sabhe-dhamma, anatta.

21
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:06,002
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's an important term, important thing.

22
00:02:07,302 --> 00:02:09,824
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how can you make it not so abstract, pretty much?

23
00:02:11,236 --> 00:02:21,759
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, just look into what's in common, to whether it's a mental formation, whether it's a determination, whether it's cetanā intention, because that's said... cetanās of sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, that's what saṅkharas are.

24
00:02:22,619 --> 00:02:23,960
[SPEAKER_00]: The Buddha said that in one of the suttas.

25
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:32,022
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what's in common is that those things are active movements, intentions, directions, pressures.

26
00:02:32,842 --> 00:02:34,283
[SPEAKER_01]: So, a form of activity.

27
00:02:35,352 --> 00:02:43,958
[SPEAKER_01]: So, activity by body, kāyā-saṅkhāra, activity of speech, vāci-saṅkhāra, activity of the mind, citta-saṅkhāra, or manu-saṅkhāra.

28
00:02:45,078 --> 00:02:46,399
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's the activities.

29
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:51,903
[SPEAKER_01]: In the broadest term, being conscious, it's the fundamental saṅkhāra.

30
00:02:52,983 --> 00:02:55,665
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already a form of activation.

31
00:02:55,685 --> 00:02:58,887
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you know, wake up, switch the power on.

32
00:02:59,488 --> 00:02:59,948
[SPEAKER_01]: You're aware.

33
00:03:00,168 --> 00:03:01,409
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're not doing anything.

34
00:03:02,571 --> 00:03:03,771
[SPEAKER_01]: But you are active.

35
00:03:03,831 --> 00:03:05,492
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how fast sankhāras go.

36
00:03:05,572 --> 00:03:09,093
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly why sankhāras determine viññāṇa in Paticca Samupādā as well.

37
00:03:10,573 --> 00:03:14,894
[SPEAKER_01]: Why sankhāras are the cause of viññāṇa to be established.

38
00:03:15,454 --> 00:03:17,574
[SPEAKER_01]: Ignorance is cause to establish sankhāras.

39
00:03:17,835 --> 00:03:19,795
[SPEAKER_01]: Sankhāras establish viññāṇa.

40
00:03:20,795 --> 00:03:23,856
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not just, I'm not doing anything, I'm free from sankhāras.

41
00:03:24,816 --> 00:03:26,937
[SPEAKER_01]: Abstaining from doing is something you're doing.

42
00:03:27,517 --> 00:03:28,457
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's your activity.

43
00:03:30,148 --> 00:03:39,692
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't escape saṅkharas by not having them, because you will be doing that, which is an activity, on the basis of you being conscious and intentional.

44
00:03:40,812 --> 00:03:43,413
[SPEAKER_01]: So, stealing of saṅkharas is a relative thing.

45
00:03:44,273 --> 00:03:50,876
[SPEAKER_01]: If you think you can just do away with them, well, you're on the level of Bodhisattva, who thought, how do I find peace?

46
00:03:51,536 --> 00:03:56,678
[SPEAKER_01]: By not doing anything, by removing doing of anything, and in the end, he wanted to even stop doing the breathing.

47
00:03:58,242 --> 00:04:02,634
[SPEAKER_01]: And then he said, but this is not... this will kill me, but there will be no, still, supreme freedom.

48
00:04:03,757 --> 00:04:06,644
[SPEAKER_01]: So then he realized, it's not about removing the activities.

49
00:04:08,542 --> 00:04:10,563
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about removing the particular aspect of them.

50
00:04:10,963 --> 00:04:22,186
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, avijjā, ignorance of that aspect of activities, is the root of all problems, not the activities, for which you need to still, and that's exactly what gradual training is.

51
00:04:22,586 --> 00:04:23,626
[SPEAKER_01]: Patimokkha is the first.

52
00:04:23,906 --> 00:04:32,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Keeping the virtue, restrained by the virtue, is the first, basically, layer of reducing the activities of the unwholesome kind.

53
00:04:33,629 --> 00:04:36,810
[SPEAKER_01]: Moderate in eating, moderating the activities that you have to do.

54
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:40,995
[SPEAKER_01]: Not distracting yourself with work, with talk, with company.

55
00:04:41,195 --> 00:04:44,940
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, moderating activities that you don't have to do, unless you have to do them.

56
00:04:46,282 --> 00:04:46,883
[SPEAKER_01]: It's seclusion.

57
00:04:47,884 --> 00:04:50,608
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just no activities of a distracting kind.

58
00:04:51,651 --> 00:04:54,613
[SPEAKER_01]: But obviously, you still are active in seclusion, you know.

59
00:04:54,753 --> 00:05:02,277
[SPEAKER_01]: You move, you talk, well, maybe not talk to yourself or something, but you move, you think, you intend, you plan, all of that.

60
00:05:02,738 --> 00:05:10,883
[SPEAKER_01]: But now those activities can become more obvious, more discernible, because you're in seclusion, not distracted by coarser activities.

61
00:05:11,103 --> 00:05:14,605
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly the process of still in the saṅkhara, guarding the sense doors,

62
00:05:16,052 --> 00:05:21,978
[SPEAKER_01]: The ultimate preventing from sort of spilling into the unwholesome domain, into the domain of the unwholesome activities.

63
00:05:26,001 --> 00:05:26,662
[SPEAKER_01]: So the...

64
00:05:29,805 --> 00:05:32,908
[SPEAKER_01]: So the whole point there, it's not like, I'll just stop doing everything.

65
00:05:34,337 --> 00:05:49,081
[SPEAKER_01]: It's more like just to see the relationship between wholesome activities, and not going into the unwholesome activities, and then fundamentally to see that aspect that you are ignorant of, in regard to the activities, that will free you from activities and all the suffering.

66
00:05:50,082 --> 00:05:53,323
[SPEAKER_01]: And that aspect is ownership of the activities.

67
00:05:55,183 --> 00:05:57,744
[SPEAKER_01]: The fundamental activity of taking things as mine.

68
00:05:59,605 --> 00:06:01,025
[SPEAKER_00]: Taking things as belonging to me.

69
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:04,011
[SPEAKER_01]: That's that's also another thing you do.

70
00:06:04,151 --> 00:06:10,555
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha called it mamankāra, mind making, ahankāra, I'm making.

71
00:06:11,275 --> 00:06:14,197
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not on the level of I choose to make this mine.

72
00:06:14,738 --> 00:06:18,820
[SPEAKER_01]: It's on the level of being conscious towards things as if they are yours.

73
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,081
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's very subtle saṅkhara, of course.

74
00:06:21,962 --> 00:06:25,844
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you have been practicing the gradual training, it would be the most obvious thing.

75
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:28,146
[SPEAKER_01]: You take things as mine.

76
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:31,468
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what why you are, not other way around.

77
00:06:32,482 --> 00:06:36,724
[SPEAKER_01]: The activities are there, that's why you have sense of self, not other way around.

78
00:06:37,584 --> 00:06:40,305
[SPEAKER_01]: Usually it's I am, I'm active, I'm inactive.

79
00:06:41,746 --> 00:06:45,267
[SPEAKER_01]: I am, things are mine or not mine if I relinquish them.

80
00:06:45,287 --> 00:06:45,447
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

81
00:06:46,287 --> 00:06:48,068
[SPEAKER_01]: Things are yours, that's already activity.

82
00:06:48,288 --> 00:06:55,651
[SPEAKER_01]: Activities are already there, you're already taking them implicitly as to you, for you, thus that's why you have a sense of self.

83
00:06:57,538 --> 00:07:02,482
[SPEAKER_01]: So you don't steal the activities because the magical peace will happen while saṅkhara subside.

84
00:07:02,602 --> 00:07:02,762
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

85
00:07:03,362 --> 00:07:05,504
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no stealing of activities in that sense.

86
00:07:06,044 --> 00:07:12,830
[SPEAKER_01]: Saṃsāra is the fundamental activity of perpetually active wandering on and on and on.

87
00:07:13,130 --> 00:07:13,830
[SPEAKER_01]: And it never ends.

88
00:07:14,431 --> 00:07:15,351
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter what you do.

89
00:07:16,212 --> 00:07:26,200
[SPEAKER_01]: Unless you remove the ownership of those neutral activities that you have discerned on account of withdrawing yourself from every single unwholesome activity on the body, speech and mind.

90
00:07:29,098 --> 00:07:33,281
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when that's discerned enough, there is no more sense of I am taking these things up.

91
00:07:33,381 --> 00:07:34,782
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no ahaṅkāra, mamaṅkāra.

92
00:07:34,822 --> 00:07:36,923
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no avijjā in regard to saṅkhāra.

93
00:07:37,844 --> 00:07:38,845
[SPEAKER_01]: So, saṅkhāras are gone.

94
00:07:39,665 --> 00:07:48,292
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the activities that are left are the activities on account of this conscious body and name and form externally for an ārahant, and he knows when that breaks apart, when that exhausts itself,

95
00:07:49,952 --> 00:07:50,732
[SPEAKER_01]: That will be the end of it.

96
00:07:51,092 --> 00:07:52,033
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the ownership is...

97
00:07:52,093 --> 00:07:57,195
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the true stilling, the true samādhi, is the removal of that sense of self in regard to activities.

98
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:58,935
[SPEAKER_01]: To remove that taking up his mind.

99
00:07:59,736 --> 00:08:02,837
[SPEAKER_01]: To remove that self-centeredness being put first.

100
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:10,980
[SPEAKER_01]: And seeing sabhe-saṅkhara-anicca, sabhe-saṅkhara-dukkha, thus self-centeredness of dhamma, is all not self-centered anymore.

101
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:12,741
[SPEAKER_01]: sabhe-dhamma-anatta.

102
00:08:13,861 --> 00:08:18,263
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the first jhāna is the basis for that complete uprooting of the sense of self.

103
00:08:19,142 --> 00:08:21,443
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the first basis of the first non-activity.

104
00:08:21,803 --> 00:08:24,164
[SPEAKER_01]: Abiding in non-activities is a synonym for jhāna.

105
00:08:25,724 --> 00:08:29,586
[SPEAKER_01]: But then the Buddha said, but when I'm in jhāna, when I walk, sit, go to toilet...

106
00:08:30,406 --> 00:08:32,286
[SPEAKER_01]: So, oh, so there are activities in jhāna.

107
00:08:32,827 --> 00:08:34,207
[SPEAKER_01]: So what isn't in jhāna?

108
00:08:34,887 --> 00:08:37,708
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, Chula Veda Lasutta says in Majjhima Nikaya, what isn't there?

109
00:08:38,549 --> 00:08:42,770
[SPEAKER_01]: Sister Damodina, the nun, she says, the sense of I am is not there.

110
00:08:44,767 --> 00:08:50,750
[SPEAKER_01]: One who is in first jhāna does not think, I am in the first jhāna, I enter the first jhāna, I exit the first jhāna, I shall be this long.

111
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:52,011
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no sense of I am.

112
00:08:52,491 --> 00:08:56,373
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no akhaṅkāra being pre-made, that's now there, being self-centered.

113
00:08:57,133 --> 00:09:02,536
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just saṅkharas, that from that point of view of ownership, are thoroughly left alone, inactive.

114
00:09:04,277 --> 00:09:10,820
[SPEAKER_01]: And she said, she also answered in the same question, she said, it's because one's mind has been developed beforehand,

115
00:09:12,063 --> 00:09:25,408
[SPEAKER_01]: Through stilling of that taking-things-as-mine on the basis of complete virtue and gradual training and withdrawal and seclusion, the mind enters or the mind basically abides in a state of not taking things as I am, even on the level of thought.

116
00:09:25,908 --> 00:09:28,349
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have thinking and pondering purified from ownership.

117
00:09:28,969 --> 00:09:32,772
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, well, then you start seeing that impersonal, the body as an impersonal.

118
00:09:32,832 --> 00:09:34,033
[SPEAKER_01]: That is already exactly.

119
00:09:34,153 --> 00:09:38,817
[SPEAKER_01]: The experience of, in the first jhāna, everything is impersonal, top to bottom, wherever you look.

120
00:09:38,897 --> 00:09:40,118
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what the Buddha did encourage.

121
00:09:40,799 --> 00:09:43,741
[SPEAKER_01]: He said that the base for arhantship is the first jhāna, or higher,

122
00:09:44,653 --> 00:09:47,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, he said, how is it so?

123
00:09:48,156 --> 00:10:08,552
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, for a monk who is in the first jhāna, if he then regards everything in that first jhāna as perilous, as dark, everything that's very wholesome, everything not taking itself, regard it in a way that it's not wanted, then his consciousness completely turns away from any basis, and that's a complete freedom.

124
00:10:09,539 --> 00:10:19,887
[SPEAKER_01]: But you won't be able to so purely regard things, see them in their nature as that, as debt, as not worth having, if you're still self-centered, if there is still conceit.

125
00:10:20,407 --> 00:10:21,808
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, if you're not in the first jhāna.

126
00:10:22,729 --> 00:10:35,478
[SPEAKER_01]: So, first jhāna, walking, standing, laying down, eating, going to toilet, seclusion, active, very active, yet completely abiding in non-activity of taking things as mine.

127
00:10:36,852 --> 00:10:42,919
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's also completely opposite of any notion of... Because, see, people do have this recognition of stealing the saṅkharas.

128
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:44,761
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, people read the suttas.

129
00:10:44,821 --> 00:10:47,164
[SPEAKER_01]: There's that sutta that says, how do you steal them?

130
00:10:47,184 --> 00:10:49,807
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, imagine you're walking, you ask yourself, why am I walking so fast?

131
00:10:49,827 --> 00:10:50,488
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me slow down.

132
00:10:51,329 --> 00:10:52,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Why don't I stand?

133
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:54,053
[SPEAKER_01]: Why don't I sit down?

134
00:10:54,513 --> 00:10:55,294
[SPEAKER_01]: Why don't I lay down?

135
00:10:55,754 --> 00:11:01,415
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is this whole kind of pretty much infinite layers of how much is still the activities.

136
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:07,637
[SPEAKER_01]: But not as a goal in itself, and not as something that will lead you then to a magical revelation of the goal.

137
00:11:08,497 --> 00:11:09,837
[SPEAKER_01]: You won't find that in the suttas.

138
00:11:10,758 --> 00:11:13,979
[SPEAKER_01]: But most people's techniques and meditation practices is exactly that.

139
00:11:14,139 --> 00:11:18,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Activities that they do with an underlying view that this will result

140
00:11:19,847 --> 00:11:20,928
[SPEAKER_01]: Give me the result.

141
00:11:21,649 --> 00:11:24,731
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the fundamental principle of the activity of sensuality.

142
00:11:25,632 --> 00:11:32,378
[SPEAKER_01]: I work, I earn, I protect, I gain, I enjoy, I engage, and I get pleasure as a reward.

143
00:11:33,278 --> 00:11:47,391
[SPEAKER_01]: And there's a sutra which says what is the danger... Well, different sutras were talking about the danger of sensuality, what it is, but in this particular one, it says the danger of sensuality is here a man recognizes, oh, because I'm attached and dependent

144
00:11:48,298 --> 00:11:55,762
[SPEAKER_01]: On the pleasure of the senses, you know, pleasure of having wife, kids, everything else, I am burdened.

145
00:11:56,962 --> 00:11:58,763
[SPEAKER_01]: I am basically...

146
00:11:58,983 --> 00:12:05,566
[SPEAKER_01]: I suffer under the pressure of duty for work, earning, protecting, worrying, providing.

147
00:12:06,587 --> 00:12:17,752
[SPEAKER_01]: All those duties are now not optional for you, because of your dependence on the pleasure that you get on account of the senses, that requires your engagement on all this high level of

148
00:12:18,349 --> 00:12:21,211
[SPEAKER_01]: Providing, worrying, constantly moving to be there.

149
00:12:21,391 --> 00:12:25,693
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you slow down, these things will go away and then immense suffering will happen.

150
00:12:26,173 --> 00:12:27,654
[SPEAKER_01]: Because your mind is dependent on it.

151
00:12:28,014 --> 00:12:36,359
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he realizes the danger of depending on the sensuality is all the pressure, the work, the burden of all these activities, they become unavoidable then.

152
00:12:37,059 --> 00:12:40,281
[SPEAKER_01]: The only way to avoid them is to remove your dependence on the pleasure.

153
00:12:42,582 --> 00:12:47,005
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly why you have to have been withdrawn from that type of dependence for a long time.

154
00:12:47,923 --> 00:12:54,568
[SPEAKER_01]: Before you can even start approaching the first jhāna in that true impersonal sense, seeing these activities on the level that they should be seen.

155
00:12:56,950 --> 00:13:02,074
[SPEAKER_01]: And these neutral activities I'm talking about, it's exactly what we've been talking about just in different terms in all these talks.

156
00:13:02,554 --> 00:13:09,179
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, like finding an impersonal anchor, the body there, underneath your currently emotionally engaged activity.

157
00:13:10,364 --> 00:13:13,305
[SPEAKER_00]: Or this, that, worry, hindrances, whatever else.

158
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:20,068
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is constantly undermined and underlined by the physicality of the body, you know.

159
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:22,829
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I'm so worried and I'm thinking about it.

160
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:28,172
[SPEAKER_01]: But look, all these activities the body is doing that I'm completely unaware of, or if I'm aware of it, I'm putting it second.

161
00:13:28,292 --> 00:13:29,392
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm putting my worry first.

162
00:13:30,153 --> 00:13:31,033
[SPEAKER_01]: I am first.

163
00:13:31,693 --> 00:13:33,154
[SPEAKER_01]: What concerns me is first.

164
00:13:33,514 --> 00:13:34,034
[SPEAKER_01]: This is second.

165
00:13:34,054 --> 00:13:34,535
[SPEAKER_01]: This is irrelevant.

166
00:13:34,555 --> 00:13:38,056
[SPEAKER_01]: Why would I... Then people sometimes might recognize, oh, actually, no.

167
00:13:38,636 --> 00:13:39,797
[SPEAKER_01]: Be mindful of the body.

168
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:41,671
[SPEAKER_01]: It's how you calm your mind.

169
00:13:42,351 --> 00:13:47,733
[SPEAKER_01]: But then they take that mindfulness in that directly active I am doing the mindfulness of the body sense.

170
00:13:49,074 --> 00:13:55,337
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means that will now be undermined and underlined by the actual peripheral physicality of the body.

171
00:13:55,957 --> 00:13:56,658
[SPEAKER_00]: Which they're not seeing.

172
00:13:56,838 --> 00:14:00,900
[SPEAKER_01]: Which they're not seeing, because now they make it a thing of I am mind doing this.

173
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:02,220
[SPEAKER_01]: It's important for me.

174
00:14:02,901 --> 00:14:07,263
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where your meditation, practice, mindfulness, whatever else, is just mechanical observances.

175
00:14:07,843 --> 00:14:11,025
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the only way to see it is, as we've been saying many times, is peripherally.

176
00:14:11,506 --> 00:14:15,289
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever's there, you're engaged with your sense of self, with your sense of ownership.

177
00:14:15,869 --> 00:14:23,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Peripheral to that, you discern the body, you know, emitting sounds, noises, sweating, tired, laying, positions, all these activities.

178
00:14:24,395 --> 00:14:27,578
[SPEAKER_01]: Reviewing the organs, the Buddha encourages, it's the same purpose.

179
00:14:28,098 --> 00:14:31,260
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a medical examination or some, again, mystical release.

180
00:14:31,361 --> 00:14:31,481
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

181
00:14:32,061 --> 00:14:36,765
[SPEAKER_01]: Peripherally, see that while you're so deeply concerned about something or related,

182
00:14:37,425 --> 00:14:43,689
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the fleshy, beating heart, skin, nose, enduring there, in this lump, a sack.

183
00:14:43,889 --> 00:14:44,850
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, behind everything.

184
00:14:44,910 --> 00:14:48,132
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, filled with various types of beings, like the simile there.

185
00:14:48,152 --> 00:14:49,893
[SPEAKER_01]: Look at these types of beings, and that types of beings.

186
00:14:50,673 --> 00:14:58,979
[SPEAKER_01]: Behind everything, moving, living on its own, not even aware that there is you, such and such, there, concerned about things.

187
00:14:59,299 --> 00:15:05,543
[SPEAKER_01]: And whatever you might be concerned, or go for, or reject, or rejoice in, is second to the physicality of a

188
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:11,724
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, living, operating body, subject to elements and everything else.

189
00:15:11,884 --> 00:15:12,525
[SPEAKER_00]: It's second to it.

190
00:15:13,426 --> 00:15:17,810
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter how self-important you are, it's second to the physicality of that sack of skin.

191
00:15:18,911 --> 00:15:19,811
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be otherwise.

192
00:15:19,992 --> 00:15:21,573
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you stop and think about it, you realize.

193
00:15:21,933 --> 00:15:26,737
[SPEAKER_01]: But the reason why people don't understand it, is because when they stop and think about it, they overdo it.

194
00:15:26,797 --> 00:15:28,019
[SPEAKER_01]: They make it into a thing.

195
00:15:28,099 --> 00:15:32,823
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't see it on the right level, which is peripheral level, which is where the level of mindfulness is.

196
00:15:34,655 --> 00:15:36,278
[SPEAKER_00]: Impersonal activity happening.

197
00:15:36,318 --> 00:15:36,638
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

198
00:15:36,778 --> 00:15:37,960
[SPEAKER_01]: Impersonal activity.

199
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:44,770
[SPEAKER_01]: Activities that have no āhankāra and māmākāra level of activation are there.

200
00:15:45,371 --> 00:15:46,393
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't see the connection?

201
00:15:47,596 --> 00:15:50,077
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're self-centered and those are the activities that matter to you.

202
00:15:50,417 --> 00:16:10,426
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whether you do your ānāpānasati or satipaṭṭhāna, doing it, doing it, doing it, while peripherally, there are all these impersonal activities that could serve as a perfect anchor for complete removal of ownership and complete vijja of saṅkhara, which would then remove the dependence of consciousness on the level of activity and it would free you from suffering.

203
00:16:12,127 --> 00:16:13,747
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why people depend on activities.

204
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:17,369
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people are afraid of solitude and inactivity and so on.

205
00:16:19,209 --> 00:16:21,531
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the consciousness depends on a certain level of engagement.

206
00:16:21,731 --> 00:16:24,513
[SPEAKER_01]: Engagement, another form of activity, another form of saṅkhara.

207
00:16:26,494 --> 00:16:34,681
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to find the impersonal activities that are occurring all the time, regardless of your mental state, hindrance, your intentions.

208
00:16:35,061 --> 00:16:36,682
[SPEAKER_00]: Feelings, just feeling, feeling.

209
00:16:36,702 --> 00:16:37,222
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, exactly.

210
00:16:37,242 --> 00:16:41,326
[SPEAKER_01]: See, in and out breathing is activity of the body.

211
00:16:42,667 --> 00:16:43,707
[SPEAKER_01]: Neutral activity of the body.

212
00:16:43,907 --> 00:16:44,468
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an activity.

213
00:16:44,668 --> 00:16:46,910
[SPEAKER_01]: But activity, as the Buddha said, it does not tire you out.

214
00:16:48,021 --> 00:16:50,342
[SPEAKER_01]: And does not bring unwholesome things to increase.

215
00:16:50,742 --> 00:16:51,622
[SPEAKER_01]: It actually makes them decrease.

216
00:16:52,062 --> 00:16:53,223
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's an activity of the body.

217
00:16:54,483 --> 00:16:57,024
[SPEAKER_01]: You can engage with it, so to learn how to see it peripherally.

218
00:16:59,005 --> 00:17:02,946
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said before, you find your breath underneath, so to speak.

219
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:05,387
[SPEAKER_01]: Thinking and pondering is the activity.

220
00:17:06,847 --> 00:17:08,748
[SPEAKER_01]: Vāci-saṅkhāra, the activity of the speech.

221
00:17:10,628 --> 00:17:13,689
[SPEAKER_01]: It's impossible to speak unless thinking and pondering is active.

222
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:15,330
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just inconceivable.

223
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:25,598
[SPEAKER_01]: And fundamentally, feeling, perception, coming and going, arising on its own, are the activities of the heart, of citta.

224
00:17:27,019 --> 00:17:28,020
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what defines citta.

225
00:17:28,241 --> 00:17:29,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Citta is the activities of that kind.

226
00:17:29,842 --> 00:17:37,710
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you remove ignorance, ownership of feelings and perceptions in the broadest sense, your citta basically has been freed.

227
00:17:39,078 --> 00:17:40,639
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the activities cannot cause you suffering.

228
00:17:40,659 --> 00:17:43,561
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why presence of activity means presence of dukkha.

229
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,682
[SPEAKER_01]: Sābe, sankhāra, dukkha.

230
00:17:46,282 --> 00:17:46,903
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter what.

231
00:17:47,543 --> 00:17:48,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter how refined sankhāra.

232
00:17:50,224 --> 00:17:51,105
[SPEAKER_00]: The activity of mind.

233
00:17:51,125 --> 00:17:51,765
[SPEAKER_00]: The activity.

234
00:17:51,965 --> 00:17:52,546
[SPEAKER_01]: The activity.

235
00:17:52,646 --> 00:17:53,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, exactly.

236
00:17:54,107 --> 00:17:54,507
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind-making.

237
00:17:54,527 --> 00:18:02,532
[SPEAKER_01]: But for somebody who is not free from eye-making and mind-making, every activity implies eye-making and mind-making, because that's the fundamental activity based on avijjā.

238
00:18:03,372 --> 00:18:07,755
[SPEAKER_01]: You remove avijjā, you remove eye-making and mind-making activity from the mind,

239
00:18:08,556 --> 00:18:10,077
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you can't say activity is there.

240
00:18:11,758 --> 00:18:15,861
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the Buddha, from Putujana's point of view, arahant, saṅkharas have ceased.

241
00:18:16,441 --> 00:18:22,164
[SPEAKER_01]: Because for Putujana's point of view, there is no other type of saṅkhara that is not rooted in ahankara and mamankara.

242
00:18:22,505 --> 00:18:25,326
[SPEAKER_01]: If it were, exactly, he would be at least a sotāpanna.

243
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:35,733
[SPEAKER_01]: But yes, arahant still talks, walks, perceives, does things by body, by speech, by mind.

244
00:18:37,402 --> 00:18:38,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, there are no saṅkharas.

245
00:18:39,203 --> 00:18:41,163
[SPEAKER_01]: So, relatively speaking, there are no saṅkharas.

246
00:18:42,284 --> 00:18:47,005
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, that's why, like, I was considering translating saṅkharas as activities.

247
00:18:49,346 --> 00:18:54,348
[SPEAKER_01]: Activity slash activation, I suppose, but you do want to have that emphasis on that.

248
00:18:54,708 --> 00:18:57,529
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a random activity of a rolling stone or something.

249
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:02,811
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the activities that are based on intentional action, because intention is another form of activity.

250
00:19:04,132 --> 00:19:05,392
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the fundamental activity.

251
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:10,733
[SPEAKER_01]: Practically speaking, every consciousness is intentional.

252
00:19:12,593 --> 00:19:13,654
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a separate thing.

253
00:19:14,414 --> 00:19:16,854
[SPEAKER_01]: And when the Buddha said, what are the determinations?

254
00:19:16,874 --> 00:19:20,155
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, it's the intentions of sight, sound... What is the aggregate of determinations?

255
00:19:20,615 --> 00:19:23,376
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, it's the intentions of sight, sound, smell, taste, touches.

256
00:19:23,736 --> 00:19:26,617
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the aggregate of activities.

257
00:19:26,637 --> 00:19:27,957
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the aggregate of saṅkharas.

258
00:19:28,857 --> 00:19:31,178
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the aggregate of determinations, whatever you translate it.

259
00:19:32,278 --> 00:19:35,279
[SPEAKER_01]: So, saṅkharas are the intentions of sight, sound, smell, taste, touches.

260
00:19:37,438 --> 00:19:40,760
[SPEAKER_01]: The intentions of your senses?

261
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:41,061
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry?

262
00:19:42,022 --> 00:19:43,963
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, they are actually the intentions of your senses.

263
00:19:44,363 --> 00:19:48,827
[SPEAKER_01]: But for a mind that's not free from avijjā, mind-making, eye-making is what's first.

264
00:19:49,348 --> 00:19:53,071
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, even when these intentions come, you have not created them, they are yours.

265
00:19:53,511 --> 00:19:58,696
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why people are, by default, moved by what they see, hear, smell, taste, touch.

266
00:19:59,978 --> 00:20:02,759
[SPEAKER_01]: And immediately assume the ownership and immediately assume engagement.

267
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:25,566
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why, again, the gradual training, withdrawal from that... You still have I-making and mind-making and so on, but you are withdrawing from that automatic kind of assumption and action out of assumed ownership, towards Saitam's Maltese touches, so that you get to see then, if you've withdrawn sufficiently enough, you get to see that I-making and mind-making as adhetstha.

268
00:20:26,867 --> 00:20:27,707
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop doing that.

269
00:20:28,709 --> 00:20:29,570
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything else is fine.

270
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:32,412
[SPEAKER_00]: Can be left alone, like a tree stump killed at the root.

271
00:20:33,113 --> 00:20:34,574
[SPEAKER_00]: You start seeing the creature.

272
00:20:35,495 --> 00:20:36,877
[SPEAKER_01]: You start seeing creature, exactly.

273
00:20:37,017 --> 00:20:39,038
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what that nun said to Mahārāja, wasn't she?

274
00:20:39,239 --> 00:20:40,580
[SPEAKER_01]: When he was talking about, what are you doing?

275
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:42,121
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, who are you talking, who are you referring to?

276
00:20:42,181 --> 00:20:46,025
[SPEAKER_01]: There is only saṅkharas manifesting and enduring, basically.

277
00:20:47,443 --> 00:20:51,906
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, she's not even seeing any of these activities even as a as a coarser form of self.

278
00:20:51,926 --> 00:20:53,767
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's like some probably some traces of conceit.

279
00:20:53,827 --> 00:20:56,748
[SPEAKER_01]: She must have been anāgāmī or, you know, very close to arahantship.

280
00:20:57,149 --> 00:20:58,729
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's just saṅkharas coming and going.

281
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:02,752
[SPEAKER_01]: Just activities manifesting and then new activities manifesting and so on.

282
00:21:03,772 --> 00:21:13,338
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's important to not fall into view... Well, it's important actually to step outside of the view, because most people abide in that view, whereby you think that, okay, so I just stop everything and that's how I stop.

283
00:21:13,478 --> 00:21:14,879
[SPEAKER_01]: That's another activity.

284
00:21:15,659 --> 00:21:15,759
[SPEAKER_01]: Cho

285
00:21:18,822 --> 00:21:23,026
[SPEAKER_01]: Choosing to not intend this or that is what you're intending right there and then.

286
00:21:23,626 --> 00:21:26,448
[SPEAKER_01]: Abstaining from these particular choices is my choice.

287
00:21:27,309 --> 00:21:37,097
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why there is no... you can't remove the saṅkharas, as in to make them not be there, and you cannot possibly act your way out of action.

288
00:21:38,939 --> 00:21:39,099
[SPEAKER_01]: So...

289
00:21:39,378 --> 00:21:42,799
[SPEAKER_01]: The kāma, good kāma, bad kāma, sure, but kāma is always going to be there.

290
00:21:43,519 --> 00:21:48,481
[SPEAKER_01]: Unless you remove that ownership on the fundamental level of intention and consciousness and your thought.

291
00:21:49,061 --> 00:21:50,462
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't, yeah, you can't decide.

292
00:21:51,042 --> 00:21:55,224
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't decide that, because that's a very, very strong, very coarse form of activity.

293
00:21:57,504 --> 00:22:00,665
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, like, you can... something's moving really fast.

294
00:22:01,446 --> 00:22:01,846
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know.

295
00:22:02,006 --> 00:22:02,346
[SPEAKER_01]: Get this.

296
00:22:02,786 --> 00:22:05,007
[SPEAKER_01]: So, my hands are very active, my hands are very active.

297
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:11,203
[SPEAKER_01]: So now is still the movement, but this is now my activity.

298
00:22:12,705 --> 00:22:18,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, so it's a relative stillness in regards to doing this with these leaves.

299
00:22:18,952 --> 00:22:24,678
[SPEAKER_01]: Relative stillness, but it's still an activity, because if I stop holding on to the leaf, it's gonna start moving again.

300
00:22:26,935 --> 00:22:33,819
[SPEAKER_01]: So, don't have the view to expect that you just rigidly stop everything and that's how you enter the peace of non-activity, because that's going to be your activity.

301
00:22:34,259 --> 00:22:51,909
[SPEAKER_01]: And whoever committed to those intense, sort of, focusing, controlling meditation techniques, well, if they're self-honest, they would see that initially they got the peace from that relative stilling, and after a while, all they were getting is frustration and trying to get that peace back, and they were getting more wound up and more intense.

302
00:22:52,489 --> 00:22:53,950
[SPEAKER_01]: And I know from my own experience.

303
00:22:54,708 --> 00:22:56,009
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm still a layman, you know.

304
00:22:56,049 --> 00:23:05,814
[SPEAKER_01]: You try everything, you don't know what's right or wrong, and yeah, you start doing this technique, and then you... two days, three days, and then just... oh, the peace is gone, because now this is your reality.

305
00:23:07,595 --> 00:23:12,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop everything, stop everything, I will move slowly, I will not speak, I will never speak, I will never look at anything.

306
00:23:13,258 --> 00:23:17,621
[SPEAKER_01]: And that becomes very active thing that you're engaged with, so there's no peace.

307
00:23:20,743 --> 00:23:27,168
[SPEAKER_01]: So the peace, is true peace, of stilling saṅkharas, is the peace of removing the ownership.

308
00:23:27,668 --> 00:23:35,013
[SPEAKER_01]: So the true peace of meditation, that still the saṅkharas correctly, is the removal of the ownership of saṅkharas, not removal of saṅkharas.

309
00:23:35,494 --> 00:23:39,116
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why for the correct meditation, you need the right view.

310
00:23:39,517 --> 00:23:42,079
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to understand where the problem is.

311
00:23:42,099 --> 00:23:42,619
[SPEAKER_01]: The ownership.

312
00:23:42,759 --> 00:23:43,560
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't just do it.

313
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:46,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're doing it with ahankara and mamankara.

